> Crowding preserves selected spread, not every nondominated point

Within a processed front, each objective supplies an ascending order. Its first
and last points receive infinite crowding; interior points add the normalized
gap between their two objective neighbors. Boundary infinities remain, and a
zero objective range skips its divisions after endpoints are marked. Thus
tied/constant objectives can designate arbitrary equal-valued endpoints; no
geometric uniqueness or density-estimation guarantee follows.

Survival fills complete fronts until its capacity is reached. If a final front
is too large, it retains only its largest crowding values. The six points below
are all mutually nondominated, but capacity four necessarily removes two. This
directly corrects the old assertion that a globally nondominated solution can
never be lost. This optimizer stores no external unlimited archive. Exact
equal-crowding ties follow the standard library’s unspecified sort ordering.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/nsga_truncation.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/optim/nsga2.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto t =
        dm::optim::nsga2_survival_trace(dm::optim::nsga2_truncation_points(), 4);
    auto &r = t.combined.ranking;
    std::vector<bool> kept(r.points.size());
    for (auto i : t.selected)
        kept[i] = true;
    std::vector<double> kx, ky, rx, ry;
    std::print("| original ID | actual rank | actual processed crowding | selected |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: " "| --- |\n");
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < r.points.size(); ++i) {
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", i, r.ranks[i], r.crowding[i],
                   bool(kept[i]));
        if (kept[i]) {
            kx.push_back(r.points[i].objectives[0]);
            ky.push_back(r.points[i].objectives[1]);
        } else {
            rx.push_back(r.points[i].objectives[0]);
            ry.push_back(r.points[i].objectives[1]);
        }
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.points(rx, ry, "removed rank0", {148, 163, 184}, 7).points(
        kx, ky, "selected rank0", {36, 105, 172}, 6).title(
        "All six points are nondominated; only four can survive").x_label(
        "objective1").y_label("objective2").save_svg("build/nsga_truncation.svg");
    std::print("\nActual survivor order {}.\n", t.selected);
}
```
