> Retain the original30-variable ZDT1 run

The original setup uses30 variables in[0,1], population100,250 generations and
seed1. Defaults remain crossover probability.9, SBX index15, per-variable
mutation probability1/30 and mutation index20. The canonical ZDT1 fixture
computes f1=x0, g=1+9Σ_(j>0)x_j/29 and f2=g(1−sqrt(f1/g)); its analytic
efficient front has g=1 and f2=1−sqrt(f1).

The first actual initial-population callback fixes the objective count; there is
no discarded dimension probe. Total callbacks are100·251=25100. Fresh summaries
report the final nondominated count, observed f1 coverage and mean signed
vertical gap f2−(1−sqrt(f1)). This is a descriptive vertical gap, not
hypervolume, IGD, an optimizer stopping criterion or a convergence certificate.
The original every-eighth sorted point table is retained. Ordinary execution
avoids retaining a quadratic detailed history of every generation.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/nsga_original.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/optim/nsga2.hpp>
#include <datamunge/optim/moead.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    dm::optim::ZDT1Objective objective(30);
    dm::optim::NSGA2Options options;
    options.population_size = 100;
    options.max_generations = 250;
    options.seed = 1;
    auto run =
        dm::optim::NSGA2(options).run(objective, std::vector<double>(30, 0),
                                      std::vector<double>(30, 1));
    auto front = dm::optim::nsga2_sorted_front(run.front);
    auto summary = dm::optim::zdt1_front_summary(front);
    std::print("| actual front points | observed minimum f1 | observed maximum f1 | mean signed vertical " "gap | actual objective callbacks | actual ranking pairs |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | " "---: | ---: |\n| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",
               front.size(), summary.min_f1, summary.max_f1, summary.mean_gap,
               run.work.evaluations, run.work.ranking_pairs);
    std::print("\n| original every-eighth sorted index | actual f1 | actual f2 |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    std::vector<double> x, y, rx, ry;
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < front.size(); ++i) {
        x.push_back(front[i].objectives[0]);
        y.push_back(front[i].objectives[1]);
        if (i % 8 == 0)
            std::print("| {} | {} | {} |\n", i, x.back(), y.back());
    }
    for (auto &p : dm::optim::zdt1_front()) {
        rx.push_back(p.objectives[0]);
        ry.push_back(p.objectives[1]);
    }
    auto plot = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    plot.lines(rx, ry, "analytic ZDT1", {148, 163, 184}).points(
        x, y, "actual NSGA-II", {36, 105, 172}, 4).title(
        "Original NSGA-II: ZDT1,30 variables,100 parents,250 generations").x_label("objective1").y_label("objective2").save_svg("build/nsga_original.svg");
}
```
