> Inspect actual tournaments, offspring ancestry and survival

A smaller six-parent,two-variable,one-generation run makes the mechanics
observable. Each binary tournament draws two slots with replacement. Lower rank
wins; equal ranks prefer strictly larger crowding, and exact ties choose the
second draw. The two winning parents may coincide. Both SBX children mutate and
evaluate in the original order before the combined parent/offspring pool is
ranked.

The table uses actual tournament records, and the diagram uses actual first-pair
ancestry, combined-pool size and selected IDs. Processed crowding fields are
flagged explicitly: survival does not compute crowding for later fronts once
capacity is full. Such unprocessed public snapshot values are zero placeholders,
not silently asserted distances. Complete actual pair and objective-order
records remain available for the processed stages.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/nsga_generation.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/optim/nsga2.hpp>
#include <datamunge/optim/moead.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    dm::optim::ZDT1Objective objective(2);
    dm::optim::NSGA2Options options;
    options.population_size = 6;
    options.max_generations = 1;
    options.seed = 1;
    auto t = dm::optim::NSGA2(options).trace(objective, {0, 0}, {1, 1});
    auto &g = t.generations.front();
    std::print("| actual tournament | first slot | second slot | first rank | second rank | first crowding " "| second crowding | actual winner |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | " "---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < g.tournaments.size(); ++i) {
        auto &a = g.tournaments[i];
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", i, a.first,
                   a.second, a.rank_first, a.rank_second, a.crowding_first,
                   a.crowding_second, a.winner);
    }
    auto pair = g.parents.front();
    auto &a = g.combined.ranking.points[pair.first_child];
    auto &b = g.combined.ranking.points[pair.second_child];
    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    d.node("parents", {0, 0},
           std::format("Actual first parent slots\n{}, {}", pair.first_parent,
                       pair.second_parent));
    d.node("children", {8, 0},
           std::format("Actual child IDs {},{}\nf2 {:.3f} / {:.3f}",
                       pair.first_child, pair.second_child, a.objectives[1],
                       b.objectives[1]));
    d.node("survival", {16, 0},
           std::format("Actual survivors from {}\nIDs {}",
                       g.combined.ranking.points.size(), g.selected));
    d.edge("parents", "children", "shared SBX + mutation").edge(
        "children", "survival", "rank + crowding");
    d.save_svg("build/nsga_generation.svg");
    std::print("\nActual callbacks {}; captured logical units {}; actual survivor IDs {}.\n",
               t.run.work.evaluations, t.captured_entries, g.selected);
}
```
